{
  "raw": {
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964405/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems Login and apply Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher in snow and microclimate processes of cold-climate ecosystems for a 3-year fixed-term position to join us in the Faculty of Technology, Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering Unit. About the job We are seeking a postdoctoral researcher to join our team to study changes and patterns in hydrology, snow and microclimates across Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems, and to connect their dynamics to ecological processes in cold climates. We welcome applicants with backgrounds in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, physical geography, environmental science, ecosystem science or ecology, as long as you bring strong numerical and programming skills and a genuine interest in cold-climate systems. We recognise that excellent candidates come from different scientific traditions. We therefore invite applications along two complementary profiles, and encourage you to indicate in your application which profile best matches your interests and expertise. Both profiles are equally valued and will be assessed on their own merits. We also welcome candidates whose expertise and interests fall between these profiles or combine elements of both. Profile A — Snow, climate and remote sensing (technical / modelling focus). You will study snow-related processes and the impacts of climate change on them in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems by combining remote sensing tools, microclimate datasets and mechanistic models. You will utilise and develop advanced mechanistic and deep-learning models with fine-resolution satellite imagery and empirical microclimate data to understand and predict the localised effects of climate change and human impacts on cold-climate hydrology and snow. This profile suits a hydrological modeller or data scientist with a strong background in spatial datasets and analyses and deep understanding in cold-climate processes. Profile B — Snow, microclimate and ecosystems (interdisciplinary focus). You will study the dynamics and spatial patterns in snow and hydrological and microclimate conditions and link them to ecological processes in Arctic, boreal and alpine ecosystems. You will investigate how shifts in snow cover, local hydrology and microclimates propagate through cold ecosystems affecting vegetation, biodiversity and ecosystem functions. This profile suits a hydrologist, physical geographer, ecosystem scientist or ecologist with strong numerical and programming skills and an understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature. The position is linked to a project led by Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen that studies local-scale trends in snow cover duration and their ecological implications across Arctic and alpine ecosystems. The postdoctoral position is also linked to large-scale and long-term research in the water sector at the Flagship DIWA - Digital Waters , and SAFIRE - Safeguarding Biodiversity through Interdisciplinary Research on Habitat Restoration- a Profi8 programme at the University of Oulu, funded by the Research Council Finland. SAFIRE’s focus is the production of scientifically excellent and actionable knowledge on habitat restoration, especially in Arctic regions. The position is located at the Water, Energy and Environmental Engineering research unit, in the Faculty of Technology. Our water research team includes 5 research groups with a strong focus on various aspects of water engineering, including hydrological modelling, cold climate hydrology, hydrological process studies, and groundwater research. In hydrology, the research includes studies at our research stations and supersites in Finland with a unique and developing infrastructure. The position is also linked to the Arctic, Antarctic and Mountain initiative , a network of ~150 researchers across the world that works on global microclimate datasets and promotes microclimate research across disciplines. Your responsibilities The responsibilities below are tailored to your chosen profile, with shared responsibilities common to both. Shared responsibilities: Integrate remote sensing observations, climate reanalysis and microclimate data to reconstruct historical snow, hydrological and microclimate trends. Collaborate with ecologists, hydrologists and modellers to assess the impacts of hydrological and cryospheric changes on ecosystems and water resources. Publish high-quality research and contribute to open-source tools. Depending on personal interest, field work in northern Finland, Sweden and Norway is possible. Participate in doctoral supervision and education. In addition, for Profile A: Develop algorithms for fine-scale snow and hydrological mapping and modelling utilising Landsat, Sentinel and PlanetScope satellite data. Advance mechanistic, deep-learning or hybrid models that translate satellite and microclimate data into predictions of snow and hydrological change. In addition, for Profile B: Analyse how changes in snow, hydrology and microclimate propagate to ecological processes in Arctic and alpine tundra and boreal forests. Bridge physical environmental data and model outputs with ecological and biodiversity datasets and outcomes. What we offer We offer you an interesting and versatile position as part of a large and growing digital water research cluster in Finland and the SAFIRE profiling research team. We help you to grow and realise your full scientific potential and contribution. You will have the opportunity to develop professionally with the help of an experienced and enthusiastic team. You will also have access to our unique global infrastructure, where innovative studies can be initiated in collaboration with our team members. The University of Oulu offers Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits. Development and career options of the big organization. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us . Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? To succeed in the position, you are required to have: A relevant doctoral degree in hydrology, remote sensing, data science, environmental science, ecosystem science, ecology, physical geography or a related field. The doctoral degree must have been completed by the closing date for applications. The degree must have been obtained no more than 10 years ago. Ability to engage in independent scientific research. Teaching skills required for the position. Strong background in numerical modelling and data analysis. Experience with programming languages such as R, Python, Julia, Fortran or C/C++. Excellent written and spoken English. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Strong experience in scientific writing and excellent communication skills. We also appreciate the following: Experience with satellite remote sensing data and analyses. Experience with collecting and analysing drone imagery. Understanding of cold-ecosystem processes and nature, and experience linking environmental drivers to ecological or biodiversity outcomes. Experience with ecological, hydrological or microclimate field measurements in cold regions. Familiarity with high-performance computing and environments. Experience in supervision or co-supervision of doctoral researchers. International experience and networking skills. Experience in proposal writing. When assessing the candidate's merits for the position of Postdoctoral Researcher, attention will be paid to scientific excellence, such as research outputs, international scientific activities and collaboration, supervision of undergraduate students, pedagogical competence, societal relevance, impact and potential of scientific activities, and services for the academic community, as well as prior experience in working with cold-climate topics. Salary The position is a fixed-term position for 3 years, beginning on 1.12.2026 (or as soon as possible thereafter). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. The salary will be based on the level 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities, depending on your qualifications. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Typical monthly salary for a post-doctoral researcher is 3700 - 4800 € (before taxes), depending on your experience and qualifications. How to apply? Apply online at the latest by October 15, 2026 (23:59 Finnish time). The application should be written in English and include the following documents: A letter of motivation containing a short description of the research you propose to conduct in the position (max 2 pages) An academic Curriculum Vitae (max 4 pages) following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of 10 most important publications : select maximum of 10 scientific articles that highlight your research interests and competence and explain your role in them. Teaching and supervision experience (2 pages) Eligible applicants best fitting the expected research profile may be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified when the selection process is completed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Further information Assistant Professor Pekka Niittynen, pekka.niittynen@oulu.fi Associate Professor Hannu Marttila, hannu.marttila@oulu.fi Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/551 Published 16.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Oct.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968632/": {
      "title": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame",
      "description": "Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Yliopisto-opettaja, pohjoissaame Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. Haemme nyt Oulun yliopiston humanistisen tiedekunnan Giellagas-instituuttiin Yliopisto-opettajaa toistaiseksi voimassa olevaan työsuhteeseen 1.1.2027 lähtien. Giellagas-instituutilla on valtakunnallinen vastuu saamen kielten ja saamelaisen kulttuurin ylimmästä opetuksesta ja tutkimuksesta Suomessa. Instituutin saamen kielten oppiaine kouluttaa kielen asiantuntijoita saamelaisyhteisön tarpeisiin. Opinnot tarjoavat mahdollisuuksia kansainväliseen uraan Pohjoismaiden rajat ylittävällä saamelaisalueella. Saamen kielten opinnoissa on kolme linjaa: pohjoissaamen, inarinsaamen ja koltansaamen linja. Pohjoissaamen linja on tarkoitettu äidinkielisille puhujille sekä muille, joilla on hyvä pohjoissaamen taito. Lisäksi instituutissa voi suorittaa 25 opintopisteen laajuiset pohjoissaamen perusopinnot vieraana kielenä. Työtehtävät Yliopisto-opettajana opetat perus-, aine- ja syventäviä opintoja ohjaat ja tarkastat opinnäytetöitä ohjaat opiskelijoita ja neuvot opintoihin liittyvissä asioissa tutkit pohjoissaamen kieltä osallistut hallinnollisten tehtävien hoitoon Mitä tarjoamme? Tuen asiantuntevalta ja innostavalta Giellagas-instituutin työyhteisöltä, jossa pääset kehittymään ja jakamaan asiantuntemustasi. Liikunta-, kulttuuri- ja hyvinvointietuja (ePassi). Lue lisää muista työsuhde-eduistamme . Ison organisaation tarjoamat kehitys- ja uramahdollisuudet. Merkityksellisen työn ja toimintakulttuurin, jossa sinulla on vapaus työn ja muun elämän yhteensovittamiseen. Lisätietoa työskentelystä Oulun yliopistossa . Mitä etsimme? Onnistuaksesi ja viihtyäksesi tehtävässä edellytämme sinulta: Ylempää korkeakoulututkintoa saamen kielten alalta C2-tasoista kirjallista ja suullista pohjoissaamen taitoa Hyvää opetustaitoa Valmiutta tieteelliseen työhön Sujuvaa kirjallista ja suullista suomen kielen taitoa Lisäksi katsomme eduksi: Pedagoginen koulutus Laaja tehtäväalueen osaaminen Muut opetustoimessa saavutetut ansiot Yliopisto-opettajan odotetaan suorittavan kahden vuoden kuluessa työsuhteen alkamisesta vähintään 25 opintopistettä yliopistopedagogisia tai niihin rinnastettavia opintoja, ellei valitulla ole näitä opintoja suoritettuna työsuhteen alkaessa. Palkkaus Tehtävä on toistaiseksi voimassa oleva alkaen 1.1.2027 (tai sopimuksen mukaan). Tehtävä sijoittuu yliopiston palkkausjärjestelmän opetus- ja tutkimushenkilöstön vaativuustasolle 5. Lisäksi maksetaan henkilökohtaiseen suoriutumiseen perustuvaa palkanosaa, joka on enintään 50 % tehtäväkohtaisesta palkanosasta. Palkka vastaavissa tehtävissä on tyypillisesti 3800-4100 EUR/kk. Tehtävässä sovelletaan 6 kuukauden koeaikaa. Kuinka hakea? Jos kiinnostuit, haethan paikkaa rekrytointijärjestelmän kautta viimeistään 18.10.2026 . Liitä hakemukseen mukaan: Hakemuskirje CV Narratiivinen CV käyttäen annettua mallia (lisätietoja Tutkimuksen ja tutkijan arvioinnin periaatteet Oulun yliopistossa ) Julkaisuluettelo Suomen Akatemian pohjan mukaan Opetusportfolio , Oulun yliopiston ohjeiden mukaisesti Tehtävään parhaiten soveltuvat hakijat kutsutaan haastatteluun, joka pidetään etäyhteydellä tai kasvokkain. Opetustaitoa arvioidaan opetusportfolion ja opetusnäytteen perusteella. Opetustaidon arvioinnista on saatava vähintään arvosana ”hyvä” (3/5). Tulemme olemaan yhteydessä kaikkiin hakijoihin hakuprosessin aikana. Lisätietoja Jäikö jokin arveluttamaan? Ota yhteyttä: johtaja Sigga-Marja Magga, humanistinen tiedekunta, Giellagas-instituutti, sigga-marja.magga@oulu.fi, +358 50 568 5326 Sámegillii ohcamuša sáhttá lohkat dáppe. Työsuhdemuoto Toistaiseksi Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/573 Julkaistu 21.09.2026 Haku päättyy 18.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:964775/": {
      "title": "Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine",
      "description": "Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Biostatistician, Lifecourse Medicine, Faculty of Medicine Login and apply Faculty of Medicine, Clinical Medicine The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Biostatistician to join us in the Research Unit of Clinical Medicine for a fixed-term position lasting until 31 December 2029 . You will be based with the Lifecourse Medicine and Birth Cohort Research Group at the Clinical Medicine Research Unit. Our mission in the research group is to understand how exposures early in life, from the fetal period onwards, affect health and well-being during the life course, up to the next generation, and to use this information to advance lifelong health and well-being. We are in particular interested in adult and next-generation outcomes of people born preterm or small for gestational age in high and low resource settings. In our research we use various types of data including whole-population data from national social and healthcare registers from Finland and other Nordic countries and data from clinically studied children and adults in high and low resource settings, including detailed physiological measurements and omics data. About the job As a biostatistician, you will Be responsible for data management including data cleaning, harmonisation and documentation and preparation of analysis datasets of diverse data types such as social and healthcare register data, data from physiological and biochemical measurements, omics data or data collected by wearables. This work is conducted in close connection with other group members, much of it in data secure remote access environments including Findata Kapseli, Statistics Finland Fiona Centre for Scientific Computing CS Desktop or corresponding Nordic environments. The job may include visits to the Nordic and other collaborators' institutions. Contribute to the design of data management solutions to maximise work efficacy and data security. Handle data access and ethics committee applications and other regulatory requirements of use of data. Contribute to research and statistical analysis plans together with other research group members, conduct statistical analyses according to these plans and document their results and methodologies used. Provide advice and take part in training of other group members on data management and data analysis. Take part in other related activities of the research group. Actively train to learn new statistical analysis and data management methods. Depending on the interest and experience of the successful applicant, the job may also include a more active role in developing scientific research questions and writing scientific papers. What we offer Working in one of the globally leading teams studying lifelong outcomes of preterm birth and related traits. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being, and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits. Work-life balance. Development and career options of the big organisation. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu ! Who are you? In order to succeed and enjoy the position, we require from you: A Masters degree in a relevant field including, but not limited to, statistics, mathematics, or bioinformatics. Fluency in written and spoken English Very good familiarity with at least one commonly used statistical software and ability to support and work with group members working with different statistical software. Experience in data management and statistical analysis in research using large quantitative datasets. Good communication and work organisation skills . We also appreciate A doctoral degree. Finnish language skills. The working language of the research group is English, but documentation including that of the data regulatory authorities may be in Finnish. Scientific contributions including scientific publications. The final job description will be shaped according to the skills and interests of the successful candidate. Salary The position is fixed term starting from 1.12.2026 (or as agreed) until 31.12.2029. The salary will be based on the levels MV08-MV09 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). Starting gross salary will be approx. 3300-4200 EUR per month (before taxes), depending on experience. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 1.11.2026 through our recruitment system. Please attach a Cover letter CV Brief description (maximum one page), in your own words, why you apply and how you meet the requirements of this position . The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. Interviews will be held during the latter half of October. The selection process may include more than one interview and a suitability assessment. The shortlisted candidates are also asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, such as people of different ages, genders, and linguistic, cultural, or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Professor Eero Kajantie, eero.kajantie@oulu.fi , Tel +358 50 473 9438. Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/554 Contact Eero Kajantie, +358504739438, eero.kajantie@oulu.fi Published 23.Sep.2026 Last application date 01.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:972279/": {
      "title": "Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team",
      "description": "Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Biostatistician, Women’s Health Team Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Lääketieteellinen tiedekunta, Kliininen lääketiede Oulun yliopisto on monitieteinen, kansainvälisesti toimiva tiedeyliopisto, jonka noin 4000 työntekijää tuottavat korkeatasoiseen tutkimukseen pohjautuvaa uutta tietoa ja antavat tutkimukseen perustuvaa opetusta kestävämmän, älykkäämmän ja inhimillisemmän maailman rakentamiseksi. Oulun yliopistoyhteisössä toimii kaikkiaan noin 19 000 henkilöä. Pohjoisen tiedeyhteisömme toiminta on globaalisti vaikuttavaa ja luo edellytyksiä innovaatioiden syntymiselle. Kaikkea tutkimus-, opetus- ja työyhteisötoimintaamme ohjaavat yliopistomme arvot sekä eettiset periaatteet. We are now looking for a Biostatistician to join us in Research Unit of Clinical Research for a fixed-term position lasting until 31.12.2027. The Women’s Health Team is a research group at the Faculty of Medicine, University of Oulu. The team advances lifelong gynecological and obstetric health of women and leads internationally recognized programs on women’s health burden and work ability, Polyendocrine Metabolic Ovarian Syndrome (PMOS; formerly PCOS), and hormonal contraception. About the job In this task you work as a statistical expert for the team You use and manage large register data sets (e.g. PMOS-FiRe), cohort data sets (NFBC, WENDY) and questionnaire data sets (FINNETWORK, WeWork). You are involved in all stages of research, from planning to analysis execution, managing data access permits , interpretation, visualization, and publishing Your tasks also include hands-on instruction of students and researchers in statistical analysis, data processing, and variable construction What we offer? The support of an experienced and enthusiastic team of 30 people where you can share your expertise and grow as an expert. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture and well-being and flexible multi-location and remote work opportunities. Read more about other staff benefits here. Work-life balance: we don't count Saturdays as holiday periods! Development and career options of the big organisation. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and close-ones in settling into Oulu. Work that matters! Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, excellent education system, and competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Who are you? In order to succeed in the position, we expect from you: A University degree in Statistics, Bioinformatics, Mathematics or closely related discipline Experience in statistical data analysis and modelling , as well as data management Fluency in written and spoken English Familiarity with data analysis software (especially R and SPSS, but other options such as SAS or STATA can also be suitable for the role) Ability to work independently and take responsibility for planning and delivering tasks Willingness to learn new methods A genuine interest in women’s health We also appreciate Finnish language skills Knowledge on GDPR regulation in the EU and Finland Experience in register data processing and analysis Familiarity with some of the following: Redcap, CSC environments Experience in bioinformatics is considered a plus, but is not required Your work has an impact on the daily lives of students and researchers at the University of Oulu and will also promote women’s health in general. The final job description will be shaped according to your skills and interests. Salary The position is fixed term starting from 1.12.2026 (or as agreed) until 31.12.2027. The salary will be based on the levels 8-9 of the demand level chart for other expert and support staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary for similar positions typically ranges from approx. 3300-3600 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied in the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by 25.10.2026 through our recruitment system. Please attach an application , CV , and a list of possible publications you have been involved in (describing your role as a statistical expert in each). The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on-site or remote interview. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from different backgrounds, such as people of different ages, different genders and members of different language, cultural or minority groups. Contact Information If you have any further questions, please contact Riikka Arffman, Senior Scientist, riikka.arffman@oulu.fi, +358 503506447 (on weekdays between 9 a.m.- 4 p.m.). Työsuhdemuoto Toistaiseksi Työsuhteen luonne Kokoaikainen Paikkojen lukumäärä 1 Työllisyysaste 100% Paikkakunta Oulu Maakunta Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Maa Suomi Ilmoitusnumero 2026/596 Julkaistu 23.09.2026 Haku päättyy 25.10.2026 Kirjaudu sisään ja hae työpaikkaa Jaa linkki Takaisin avoimiin työpaikkoihin Grade Varbi Recruit rekrytointijärjestelmä Evästeet Ehdot Tietosuojakäytäntö Saavutettavuusseloste × Modal title Käytämme evästeitä sisäänkirjautumiseen, käyttökokemuksen parantamiseen, jakolinkkien tarjoamiseen sekä joissakin tapauksissa markkinointiin ja tilastojen keräämiseen. Hyväksy kaikki evästeet Hyväksy vain tarpeelliset Lue lisää evästeistä tässä ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968327/": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Postdoctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Faculty of Science, Ecology and Genetics The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Postdoctoral Researcher to join us, Global Change and Biotic Interactions Ecology -group, for the Research Council of Finland-funded project “ Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change ”, both led by Prof. Anu Eskelinen ( Eskelinen Research Group | Global Change and Biotic Interaction Ecology ). Description of the position We are looking for a highly motivated and talented, strongly research-oriented person to carry out postdoctoral research addressing the mechanisms of plant biodiversity change. In this project, we investigate what are the roles of mechanisms related to spatial context, dispersal in space and time, biotic interactions (competition, herbivory) and intraspecific trait change in driving heterogeneous responses of plant biodiversity to different global change factors (e.g., climate warming, nutrient enrichment). We aim for a more holistic understanding of plant biodiversity change in the Anthropocene, being able to provide answers to questions: how, why and where plant biodiversity changes. The research questions can relate, for example, to (1) the role of seed banks as a diversity maintaining mechanism under multiple global changes, (2) the role of competition for light and other mechanisms such as litter and loss of herbivory in driving diversity loss under climatic and other global changes, and (3) the role of intraspecific trait change in modifying the effects of climatic and other global changes on plant biodiversity. These will be developed together with the project leader. The postdoctoral researcher in collaboration with the project leader and collaborators will use existing data from long-term global change experiments, analyze data, and write manuscripts/publish articles in highly reputable international journals. These data come from two experiments: (1) eDiValo experiment that was designed to test the ecological impacts of light on plant community diversity (Eskelinen et al. 2022 Nature), and (2) a long-term experiment in tundra manipulating temperature, grazing and nutrients (Kaarlejärvi et al. 2017 Nat Comm). There is also a possibility for some experimental field work, although the position is mostly targeted using already existing long-term experimental data. Other duties may include teaching in undergraduate/graduate courses and co-supervising master's and doctoral students and contributing to developing new proposals to continue further research in this area. In addition, you may have to participate in administrative tasks of the university and/or the Ecology and Genetics Unit. Although the position will be based at the Ecology and Genetics Research Unit in Oulu, the doctoral researcher will also collaborate with an international researcher team from, for example, the University of Utrecht, Netherlands, the German Centre for Integrative Biodiversity Research iDiv, Germany, and the University of Helsinki, Finland. There may also be research visit(s) to these collabortors’ groups. We also expect participation to international conferences. Qualification requirements for the Postdoctoral researcher position PhD in plant community ecology or equivalent field (obtained within the past 10 years) Demonstrated ability to prepare independently high-impact manuscripts/publications for international journals Demonstrated experience and knowledge of plant biodiversity research, experimental research, global change research, trait-based plant ecology, or some combination of these Strong statistical, data exploration and data management skills, excellent skills with software R Knowledge of grassland ecosystems (e.g., temperate, tundra) Ability for independent scientific work Open-mindedness, curiosity, strong motivation and enthusiasm towards research and science Excellent written and spoken English Good communication and teamwork skills. Assessment of the applicants will be based on, acknowledging the content of the job, 1) overall fit to the above profile, 2) scientific publications, 3) motivation, 4) previous work experience, 5) national and international mobility and networking skills, and 5) other academic activities and merits. What we offer You will become a part of a highly enthusiastic and talented research group that is working on globally significant research areas The support of an experienced and enthusiastic research team where you can share and grow your expertise. Inspiring, novel, and ambitious study questions/systems Possibility for a flexible combination of presence work and remote work (this can be negotiated, depending on the situation of the applicant and project demands) Full benefits provided by the University of Oulu to university employees, including free time corresponding to holidays and free occupational health care services. The successful candidate will also receive benefits provided by the Finnish government to residents, for example, the possibility to obtain access to the national healthcare system, tax benefits for employees with children, and high-quality affordable childcare services. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety,an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Salary The position is fixed-term for two (2) years as of February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The start date is flexible and can be negotiated. The salary will be based on the levels 5-6 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The starting gross salary will be approx. 3900-4300 € per month (before taxes). A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by November 15 , 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. Only applications sent via the online system will be considered. The application should be written in English and include the following: A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience, expertise, research interests and motivation, and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. Also, information on personal career plans are highly encouraged. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity List of publications , following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland Contact information of two senior/experienced researcher s who may be asked to give a statement on the candidate The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on- site or remote interview. The shortlisted candidates will also be asked to submit their diplomas, and their references will be contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information For further information, please contact Professor Anu Eskelinen (anu.eskelinen(at)oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/568 Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
    },
    "https://oulunyliopisto.varbi.com/en/what:job/jobID:968629/": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Swedish Norwegian Danish Finnish German Dutch Chinese (BETA) Polish French Romanian Norwegian (nynorsk) Doctoral Researcher, Ecology and Genetics Login and apply Faculty of Science, Ecology and Genetics The University of Oulu is a multidisciplinary, international research university, with about 4000 employees who produce new knowledge based on high-standards research and provide research based education to build a more sustainable, smarter, and more humane world. The University of Oulu community has about 19,000 people in total. Our northern scientific community operates globally and creates conditions for the emergence of innovations. The University of Oulu is ranked in the top 3% of the world’s universities. All our research, education, and community activities are guided by our university’s values and ethical principles. We are now looking for a Doctoral Researcher to join us, Global Change and Biotic Interactions Ecology -group, for the Research Council of Finland-funded project “ Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change ”, both led by Prof. Anu Eskelinen ( Eskelinen Research Group | Global Change and Biotic Interaction Ecology ). Description of the project We are looking for a highly motivated and research-oriented person to carry out doctoral research addressing the mechanisms of plant biodiversity change. In this project, we investigate what are the roles of mechanisms related to spatial context, dispersal in space and time, biotic interactions (competition, herbivory) and intraspecific trait change in driving heterogeneous responses of plant biodiversity to different global change factors (e.g., climate warming, nutrient enrichment). We aim for a more holistic understanding of plant biodiversity change in the Anthropocene, being able to provide answers to questions: how, why and where plant biodiversity changes. The specific research questions can relate, for example, to (1) the role of temporal dispersal via soil seed banks as a diversity maintaining mechanism under multiple global changes, (2) the role of intraspecific trait change in modifying the effects of climatic and other global changes on plant biodiversity, and (3) relative and interactive roles of spatial context (i.e., connectivity and habitat size), dispersal and herbivory in mediating plant biodiversity response to global changes. A suitable combination of these questions/ideas will be developed together with the project leader. We use already existing data (ready to be analyzed) and will also collect new data from two unique, existing long-term experimental systems to address these research questions. Your tasks As a Doctoral Researcher, you will conduct research in the “Mechanisms of Plant Biodiversity Change” project described above and complete a doctoral degree and studies studies at the University of Oulu Graduate School. Your specific tasks are: Collecting new data on plant communities (field, greenhouse and laboratory work), including organizing and planning the work Conducting plant trait measurements Conducting statistical analyses on new and already existing research data from long-term field experiments Writing manuscripts (2-3) and publishing the research findings in high-quality international peer-reviewed journals under the guidance/supervision of your mentor and in collaboration with other researchers Participating national and international conferences and workshops, when relevant Teaching in BSc/MSc level courses and co-supervising master's students and interns. Being an active member of the working group Although the position will be based at the Ecology and Genetics Research Unit in Oulu, the doctoral researcher will also collaborate with an international researcher team from, for example, the University of Helsinki, Finland and the University of California, Davis, USA. There may also be research visit(s) to these collabortors’ groups. Qualification requirements for the Doctoral researcher position MSc in plant community ecology or equivalent field Strong motivation, curiosity, and enthusiasm towards ecological research and to pursue doctoral studies Experience and interest in some of the following: plant biodiversity research, experimental research, global change research, trait-based plant ecology Excellent statistical skills with software R Ability to travel and do field work, experience in field work Good grassland plant identification skills and ability to quickly learn new species Knowledge of grassland ecosystems (e.g., temperate, tundra) Excellent written and spoken English Good communication and teamwork skills, ability to work in an international team Driver’s licence is needed or willingness to acquire one See also the requirements of the University of Oulu Graduate School (UniOGS) Assessment of the applicants will be based on, acknowledging the content of the job, 1) overall fit to the above profile, 2) scientific publications (if applicable), 3) motivation, 4) previous work experience, 5) national and international mobility and networking skills, and 5) other academic activities and merits. What we offer A three-year, full-time Doctoral Researcher position in an ambitious project Opportunities for national and international collaboration, conference participation, co- authored publications and research mobility if relevant to your doctoral project You will become a part of a highly enthusiastic and talented research group that is working on globally significant research areas Possibility for a flexible combination of presence work and remote work (this can be negotiated, depending on the situation of the applicant and project demands) Full benefits provided by the University of Oulu to university employees, including free time corresponding to holidays and free occupational health care services. The successful candidate will receive also benefits provided by the Finnish government to residents, for example possibility to obtain access to the national healthcare system, tax benefits for employees with children, and high-quality affordable childcare services. Wellness benefit ePassi covering sport, culture, and well-being. Read more about other staff benefits here. Our Buddy Programme and Spouse Network support you and your close ones in settling into Oulu. We have an HR Excellence in Research -quality label, which is a recognition awarded by the European Commission for the development of researchers’ working conditions and careers. Work that matters and a workplace that promotes flexibility and work-life balance. Read more about working with us. Finland is one of the most livable countries in the world, with a high quality of life, safety, an excellent education system, and a competitive economy. Read more about living in Oulu. Salary The position is fixed-term for three (3) years as of February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The start date is flexible and can be negotiated. The salary will be based on the levels 2-4 of the demand level chart for teaching and research staff of Finnish universities. In addition, a salary component based on personal work performance will be paid (a maximum of 50 % of the job-specific component). The typical starting gross salary will be approx. 2600-3000 € per month (before taxes). As the doctoral research progresses, there is salary progression in accordance with the University salary system. A trial period of 6 months is applied to the position. How to apply? Interested? If yes, please apply by November 15, 2026 (23:59 Finnish local time, UTC +3) through our recruitment system. Only applications sent via the online system will be considered. The application should be written in English and include the following: 1. A motivation letter (max. 2 pages) summarizing the applicant’s professional experience, and expertise, research interests and motivation, and describing why the applicant is interested in this position. The motivation letter should also include contact information of two senior/experienced researchers who may be asked to give a statement on the shortlisted candidates. 2. CV , following the guidelines of the Finnish Advisory Board on Research Integrity 3. List of publications , if applicable, following the guidelines of the Research Council of Finland 4. A copy of the relevant degree certificate or diploma ; if the qualifying degree is not yet complete, please describe your expected completion date The eligible applicants fitting best in the profile expected for the position will be invited to an on- site or remote interview. The refernces of the shortlisted candidates will also contacted. All applicants will be notified during the selection process. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, including people of different ages, genders, languages, cultures, and minority communities. Contact Information For further information, please contact Professor Anu Eskelinen (anu.eskelinen(at)oulu.fi) Type of employment Temporary position over 6 months Contract type Full time Salary TES Number of positions 1 Full-time equivalent 100% City Oulu County Pohjois-Pohjanmaa Country Finland Reference number 2026/572 Published 24.Sep.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Login and apply Share links Return to job vacancies Grade Varbi Recruit recruitment system Cookies Terms Data privacy policy Accessibility statement × Modal title We use cookies for login, improved user experience, share links and in some cases marketing and collection of statistics. Accept all cookies Accept only necessary Read more about our cookies here ×"
